{"id": "u17", "config": "router", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "text", "lang": "pa", "difficulty": "easy", "hardest": false, "category": "translation", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "R5-default", "reason": "no hard or simple cue: Sarvam-105B default effort", "detected_lang": "en", "pii_masked": 0, "router_overhead_ms": 0.186, "router_tokens": 0, "human_review": "review_queue", "holding_phrase": false, "model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 24, "out_tokens": 2102, "cost_inr": 0.05279, "latency_ms": 8439.3, "attempts": [{"model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 24, "out_tokens": 2102, "reasoning_tokens": 1595, "cost_inr": 0.05279, "latency_s": 8.439}], "reasoning_tokens": 1595, "answer": "\nHere are a few ways to translate \"Your loan EMI is due on 5 December\" into Punjabi, ranging from the most common to slightly more formal options.\n\n### Most Common Translation:\n\n**ਤੁਹਾਡੀ EMI 5 ਦਸੰਬਰ ਨੂੰ ਬਕਾਇਆ ਹੈ।**\n\n*   **Transliteration:** tuhāḍī EMI 5 disambar nūṁ bakāyā hai.\n\n---\n\n### Other Excellent Options:\n\nHere are a few variations that are also correct and widely used:\n\n**1. Using the word for \"installment\" (ਕਿਸ਼ਤ):**\n> **ਤੁਹਾਡੀ ਕਿਸ਼ਤ 5 ਦਸੰਬਰ ਨੂੰ ਬਕਾਇਆ ਹੈ।**\n> (Your installment is due on 5 December.)\n> *Transliteration: tuhāḍī kisht 5 disambar nūṁ bakāyā hai.*\n\n**2. A slightly more direct/colloquial way:**\n> **ਤੁਹਾਡੀ EMI 5 ਦਸੰਬਰ ਨੂੰ ਦੇਣੀ ਹੈ।**\n> (Your EMI is to be paid on 5 December.)\n> *Transliteration: tuhāḍī EMI 5 disambar nūṁ denī hai.*\n\n**3. The simplest way:**\n> **ਤੁਹਾਡੀ EMI 5 ਦਸੰਬਰ ਨੂੰ ਹੈ।**\n> (Your EMI is on 5 December.)\n> *Transliteration: tuhāḍī EMI 5 disambar nūṁ hai.*\n\n---\n\n### Breakdown of the Words:\n\n*   **ਤੁਹਾਡੀ (tuhāḍī):** Your (feminine, for EMI/installment)\n*   **EMI (ਈ.ਐਮ.ਆਈ.):** A commonly used acronym for \"Equated Monthly Installment.\"\n*   **ਕਿਸ਼ਤ (kisht):** The traditional Punjabi word for \"installment.\"\n*   **5 ਦਸੰਬਰ (5 disambar):** 5 December\n*   **ਨੂੰ (nūṁ) / 'ਤੇ ('te):** Both are used for \"on\" (e.g., 5 ਦਸੰਬਰ ਨੂੰ or 5 ਦਸੰਬਰ 'ਤੇ).\n*   **ਬਕਾਇਆ ਹੈ (bakāyā hai):** Is due / is outstanding.\n*   **ਦੇਣੀ ਹੈ (denī hai):** Is to be paid.", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
